11:32:52 said  I built a full Android journal app in the style of Journey that lets you write entries, automatically tag them with your location, browse them on a map and a monthly calendar, add custom tags, and pick and filter by your mood. Each entry can include photos, videos, audio recordings, and a handwritten signature, and it records the weather at the time along with your movement or step count, plus you can schedule daily reminders on the days and times you choose.
11:32:52 said  It follows what I could confirm from the original app, but some details are best-effort estimates—like the exact mood scale and how activity is measured, the exact look and behavior of every original screen, and the signature format—and it doesn’t include Journey’s online accounts or cloud sync. I couldn’t compile and test it here because the Android build tools aren’t installed on this computer, so it will need to be opened and built in an Android setup to confirm it runs.
11:32:53 said  If you’d like, I can next refine the look to match the original more closely or add extras like richer entry search, templates, or password protection.
