13:20:38 said  I studied the original Journey app thoroughly and rebuilt it as a complete Android app with the same core journaling features you asked for. It includes automatic location tagging with a browsable map view, rich attachments for photos, videos, audio recordings, and handwritten signatures, automatic weather and motion/activity logging on each entry, scheduled local reminders you can set to specific times and days, and a full monthly calendar with custom tags and mood tracking that you can filter by.
13:20:38 said  I documented what I could confirm from the original app’s behavior and carried those rules into the replica, including entry details, weather and location fields, attachments, and daily reminder timing/day rules. The app builds successfully; some parts I could not prove exactly from the original (like the exact mood scale presentation, the precise meaning of the activity value, and the original signature storage format) are handled with sensible equivalents and noted as estimates.
13:20:38 said  What differs from the original is mainly visual polish, cloud/sync and account features, and some internal behaviors that couldn’t be fully recovered, but the five core feature areas you required are all implemented. If you’d like, I can next refine the look to match the original more closely, add more reminder customization, or expand the map and calendar browsing experience.
