14:13:15 said  I built a full Android journaling app in the project workspace that mirrors the requested Journey features: you can create entries with automatic location tagging, browse them on a map and in a monthly calendar, attach photos, videos, audio files or recordings, and draw handwritten signatures, while each entry can also store weather, motion/step activity, a selectable mood, and custom tags with filtering.
14:13:15 said  It also includes scheduled daily reminders with chosen days and times that send local notifications and come back after a device restart. Because some original app details can’t be fully recovered from the package, a few parts are careful estimates in this replica—such as the exact mood scale/meaning, how the original counted activity, the original signature storage format, and some behind-the-scenes reminder and UI behaviors—though the rebuilt versions are fully usable.
14:13:16 said  If you’d like, a good next step is to test it on your phone and tell me which screen or workflow feels most different from the real Journey app so I can refine it to match more closely.
